# OS generated files #
######################
**.DS_Store*
ehthumbs.db
# NOT `Icon?`, which is what this was. macOS names its custom-folder-icon file
# "Icon" plus a carriage return, and `?` was there to match it - but `?` matches
# any fifth character, and git on a Mac is case-insensitive, so the pattern also
# swallowed includes/views/icons/. The view in there was never committed: every
# screen that rendered it worked locally and died in CI.
#
# The real name cannot be written here - git strips a trailing carriage return
# from every .gitignore line - so this catches the plain name and lets the
# exotic one show up in `git status`, which is the safer way round.
Icon
Thumbs.db
._*

# Vim generated files #
######################
*.un~

